 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to the date for filing the\ncertificate of nomination for new parties",
    "basePrintNo": "S4426",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4426-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6-128, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4426\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the election law, in relation to the\ndate for filing the certificate of nomination for new parties\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo ensure ballots are timely certified and accurate prior to the general\nelection.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends subdivision 2 of section 6-128 of the\nelection law is amended to change the deadline for filing certificates\nof nomination not later than the first day of September preceding the\ngeneral election.\n\nSection 2 of the bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPresently, a new party can file a certificate of nomination no later\nthan 7 weeks before the general electibn. The deadline to certify the\nballot and begin to prepare the general election and MOVE ballots is\nnearly 8 weeks before the general election. This change ensures that\ncertificates of nomination will be filed in time to certify the ballot.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
